{"text": "VICKI J. HUNT, JD, MPH\n\n53 Sundance Drive 505.428.8229\nSanta Fe, NM 87506 vjhunt2006@mac.com\nBAR MEMBERSHIPS: Commonwealth of Virginia (1983)\n\nDistrict of Columbia (1984)\nNew Mexico (2006)\n\nEDUCATION: George Mason University, Fairfax, VA\nBachelor of Arts in Mathematics - January 1980\n\nGeorge Mason University School of Law, Arlington, VA\nJuris Doctor - May 1983\n\nThe George Washington University, Washington, DC\nMaster of Public Health in Health Policy - May 2006\nGraduated summa cum laude\n\nMPH Special Project: \u201cCommunity Shielding \u2014 A Policy Analysis\u201d\nThe George Washington University Homeland Security Policy Institute\n\nEXPERIENCE: State of New Mexico Department of Health Office of General Counsel\n(1/10/09 to present)\n\nAssistant General Counsel\n\nServe as lead counsel providing representation to the Department of Health (DOH) Epidemiology and Response\nDivision (ERD) and the Bureau of Health Emergency Management (BHEM). Provide support for all aspects of legal\nemergency preparedness to assist in the State's and DOH's fulfillment of requirements under several federal emergency\npreparedness grants: the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) Public Health Emergency Preparedness\n(PHEP) cooperative agreement (base grant); the PHEP H1N1 grant; and the Assistant Secretary for Preparedness and\nResponse (ASPR) Hospital Preparedness Program (HPP) cooperative agreement. Respond to requests from ERD\nleadership and BHEM managers/staff for legal advice/assistance in accordance with established protocols. Develop DOH\npolicies and protocols relative to the State\u2019s emergency preparedness initiatives and consistent with federal grant\nrequirements. Review and revise as necessary State and DOH emergency preparedness and response plans (e.g., State\nEmergency Operations Plan, DOH Emergency Operations Plan, State SNS Plan, etc.) and conduct legal research to\nprovide appropriate authorities and processes for the implementation of plan provisions, public health interventions, etc.\nProvide support for the NMserves Registry, the State's system for the advance registration of health care professionals.\nAdvise ERD leadership and BHEM managers/staff on the applicability of state and federal emergency preparedness laws\nand regulations. Participate in BHEM management review of program requirements and issues related to federal\nemergency preparedness grant requirements. Review State laws/regulations to conduct gap analyses with regard to State\nemergency preparedness legislation and draft proposed amended or new legislation to fill the gaps and to satisfy federal\ngrant requirements. Provide legal training and education to ERD leadership and BHEM managers/staff on the laws,\nregulations, policies and procedures applicable to the State\u2019s emergency preparedness initiatives as well as federal\nemergency preparedness grant requirements. Serve as first tier legal counsel in the DOH Department Operations Center\n(DOC) on the on-call roster to report and provide legal advice/assistance in the event of an emergency and activation of\nthe DOC.\n\nReview all DOH contracts and agreements related to emergency preparedness. Develop, review and revise (as\nnecessary) all DOH contracts, memoranda of agreement or understanding, or intergovernmental agreements related to or\nnecessary for all programs within BHEM (planning, training and education, and HPP), including but not limited to\nprofessional services agreements for necessary procurement of services; hospital sub-grant agreements; H1N1 funding\nagreements for local and tribal governments; H1N1 provider and recipient agreements; SNS receipt, staging and storage\nagreements and point of distribution agreements, etc. Provide legal training and education to ERD leadership and BHEM",
"words": [
